6. Compile and ship
bash
gh aw compile
git add .github/workflows/project-triage.md .github/workflows/project-triage.lock.yml
git commit -m "Add project triage workflow"
git push

The .lock.yml must be committed — that's the file Actions actually runs.

7. First run

Open a test issue with a realistic title and body. Then watch it:

bash
gh run watch
gh aw logs project-triage

I'd strongly suggest doing your first run against a throwaway board, or with staged mode enabled, so a badly-calibrated prompt doesn't scribble across a board you care about. 
